hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18920","Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakkai narrated to us, he said: Mansur and al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil, he said: Subayah gave birth after the death of her husband by twenty-three or twenty-five nights, then she adorned herself, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was approached and informed, and he said: If she does, her term has passed."
"18921","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, and Affan said: Shubah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak, he said: Subayah bint al-Harith gave birth after the death of her husband by twenty-three or twenty-five nights. When she became free from postpartum bleeding, she adorned herself for marriage, so that was objected to her, and that was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: If she does, her term has become lawful. Affan said: Her term has ended."
